## P18-V01 request/reply table removal semantics — 2026-10-16T08:07Z

- The pinned Java `RequestFutureHolder` fixture now verifies that removing a
  correlation leaves the `RequestResponseFuture` latch at one and its
  independent timed wait returns null. Fixture SHA-256:
  `b5c6e39d24e197d678fd214418f4f18b4fabb9f63ef27e74d3e152c7616ef5ef`.
  Fixture commit: `aef6b86a`.
- Rust `PendingReplyRequest::receive` now retains the original deadline after
  the public live table removes, replaces, or clears its entry. Explicit
  `control.cancel` and registry clear send `Cancelled`; the waiter tracks a
  closed oneshot so a cancelled receive future can be polled again safely.
  Added fixture assertions and regressions for removal through deadline,
  registry clear, and reply/cancel arbitration. Code commit: `65becc27`.
- The first full scoped suite exposed an old assertion expecting cancellation
  to close the oneshot as an error. Updated it to assert `Cancelled`; the rerun
  passes Core (168 unit tests plus integration/doc targets), Producer (142
  unit tests plus integration/doc targets), and facade (5 request/reply
  integration tests). Strict scoped all-target/all-feature Clippy, format,
  diff checks, and pinned Maven `verify` (37 scenarios, fixture drift and
  cross-decodes) pass.
- Updated the Phase 15 request/reply matrix and release checklist. This closes
